1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,400
Why the Ottoman Empire collapsed? Simple enough for a kid to understand.

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:09,200
For 600 years, the Ottoman Empire was one of the most powerful forces on Earth.

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:13,360
It controlled three continents, sat at the center of world trade.

4
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:18,480
Then it was gone. It didn't fall to a stronger empire. It collapsed under its own weight.

5
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:24,560
The Empire ran on conquest. New territory meant new taxes, new resources, new wealth.

6
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:28,880
But by the 1700s, there was nowhere left to expand easily.

7
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:34,000
The money stopped flowing in. Meanwhile, Europe was industrializing factories,

8
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,800
railroads, modern weapons. The Ottomans were still running a medieval economy.

9
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:43,520
They borrowed money from European banks to modernize, then couldn't pay it back.

10
00:00:43,520 --> 00:00:49,760
European powers used the debt to extract concessions, trading rights, territory, influence.

11
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:54,160
Slowly, the Empire that once terrified Europe became dependent on it.

12
00:00:54,160 --> 00:00:58,320
World War I finished it. The Ottomans backed the losing side.

13
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:03,360
When Germany fell, the Empire was carved up by Britain and France in a single conference.

14
00:01:03,360 --> 00:01:07,440
Borders were drawn by European diplomats who had never visited the region.

15
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:12,720
Those borders still cause conflict today. Six centuries of power ended in an afternoon

16
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:18,240
meeting in Paris. And that's just one story inside Paladin. It's like Duolingo but for

17
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:24,320
history lovers. Addictive, smart, surprisingly fun. Try it now and become the most intelligent

18
00:01:24,320 --> 00:01:30,560
person in the room.

